{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs at c46445024fe159433844ee0d302bac0d0a9b8cbb — documentation carried to the two-screen browser view, under ratified proposal c26a7f57 (25981e55). Three pages change and no others. docs/concepts/components.md replaces the Work-board paragraph with what the resident now serves: the open-request list with its row, its priority default and its click-to-sort, the single headline number and the two quiet lines that each open to exactly the rows they count, and the thread as a vertical rail of salient stations with history behind counted expanders. It states the merge station's two sources, because the fold knows whether a commitment closed and only Git knows whether the code landed, and it states the three answers that station keeps apart — landed, absent, and could-not-be-determined — since a check that fails must not read as a negative. It also records that ordinary staleness stays quiet while world-staleness and retirement stay loud. docs/reference/architecture.md amends three rows of the package-boundary table: internal/gitstore now answers plain history questions and reports \"cannot tell\" separately from \"no\"; internal/service must preserve ordinary Git history as a fourth distinction beside kernel refusal, application interpretation, durable state and live state, and resolves the ref itself because a browser names only commits; and ui/ renders as two screens and shows both sources where the fold and Git disagree rather than choosing. docs/how-to/run-a-work-loop.md loses the \"Give a topic a stable name\" section, whose topic_title and topic_alias labels had exactly one reader, the topic grouping this head deletes. Conditions actually met at this exact head: the four docset gates pass under go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/..., so every citation resolves and no page cites a retired or missing basis; go vet, go test -count=1 ./..., and go test -race -count=1 ./... pass. Carried once onto main 8c0a2052 with no file overlap against merges 12105a30 and 44b54074, which changed docs/reference/performance.md — a file this head does not touch. Predecessor at this exact path: 836fa61f (#6942) at 8c0a2052, to be retired at merge.","body":{"commit":"c46445024fe159433844ee0d302bac0d0a9b8cbb","path":"docs"}}